SUMMARY:Corn Hole Tournament at AMB
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Social Club\n**Hey y’all!! We’re gonna host a Co
 rn Hole Tournament at Appalachian Mountain Brewery!**\n**We’re gonna hos
 t a double elimination tournament!** **AMB has four cornhole board sets\, 
 and several of us have more. We’re going to run eight games at a time if
  needed.** **Come out and let’s have some fun\,** **and support a great 
 local business!**\n\n**Grab your partner and come out and play! If you do 
 not have a partner\, you can** **partner with someone at the event.** **Do
  not let not having a partner stop you from coming out for this event.**\n
 \n**Be there at 5:00 to register teams of two\, or to find a partner at th
 e event. Registration closes at 5:45.**\n\n**https://www.amb.beer/mills-ri
 ver**\n\n**This is gonna be fun!!**\n\n**The object of cornhole is to reac
 h exactly 21 points first. Teams score points by tossing bags onto the boa
 rd (1 point) or through the hole (3 points). Play alternates until all 8 b
 ags are tossed\, and scores cancel each other out at the end of each round
  (cancellation scoring).Setup &**\n\n**GameplayDistance: Place boards 27 f
 eet apart (measured from the front edge to the front edge). For a casual b
 ackyard game\, you can adjust this distance based on player ability.**\n\n
 **Teams: Played with 2 players (Singles) or 4 players (Doubles). In double
 s\, teammates stand directly across from each other at opposite boards.**\
 n\n**Turns: Players throw underhand and must stay behind the foul line (th
 e front edge of the board). Players alternate turns throwing one bag at a 
 time until all 8 bags have been tossed.**\n\n**Scoring: in the hole: 3 poi
 nts. On the board: 1 point. Foul bag: 0 points (e.g.\, if a bag hits the g
 round first or if a player steps on or crosses the foul line).Points are c
 alculated using cancellation scoring.**\n\n**The team with the higher scor
 e in the round subtracts the lower team's score to get the net points for 
 that round. For example\, if Team A scores 5 points and Team B scores 3 po
 ints\, Team A is awarded 2 points for that frame.**
